// Project Euler 34 (reduced): numbers equal to the sum of the factorials of
// their digits. The only two are 145 and 40585; the search covers the first
// and the second is checked directly, because the full search to 50000 takes
// about twenty seconds.
isCurious(n) = sum(map(d => d!, integerDigits(n))) == n
(listFrom(filter(10..2000, isCurious)), isCurious(40585))
// ➔ ([145], True)
